    dcterms:description "This study evaluates the content quality, usability, and digital features of library websites of 26 Indian Institutes of Information Technology (IIITs). Using a 65-item checklist under seven categories, the research found that while 61.5% of features were commonly present, essential user-focused elements such as feedback forms, social media links, and Web 2.0 tools were significantly lacking. Top-performing websites included IIIT Hyderabad, IIIT Allahabad, and ABV-IIITM Gwalior. A moderate correlation (r = 0.57) was found between website quality and Scopus-indexed research output, though no si" ;
