    a lis:Article ;
    dcterms:title "A novelist among the anthropologists: Barbara Pym and the International African Institute" ;
    dcterms:issued "2025"^^xsd:gYear ;
    lis:citesCount 0 ;
    dcterms:description "The acclaimed novelist Barbara Pym worked for the International African Institute from 1948 to 1974 contributing her editing and administrative skills to the Institute’s journal, Africa, and output of scholarly publications on Africa. This article explores that contribution, her working relationships with Cyril Daryll Forde and other anthropologists, and how all this is reflected and referenced in her novels, especially in points of contact between Forde’s ethnography and Pym’s Quartet in Autumn." ;
