    dcterms:description "The British Library (BL) holds over 20,000 printed books, serials and newspapers in well over 100 languages of Africa south of the Sahara. These collections date from the seventeenth century, and continue to grow. Although not comprehensive, they reflect all the major developments in African-language publishing across the continent. This article analyses these collections in the context of the broader history of publishing in African languages, and discusses how they have been acquired. Through further analysis of the extent and composition of the collections, and how they compare to those of " ;
