    dcterms:title "Trends in authorship by women at Canadian universities 2006 to 2019" ;
    dcterms:issued "2021"^^xsd:gYear ;
    lis:citesCount 2 ;
    dcterms:description "Despite much progress since the mid-20th century, there still exists a disparity in the number of female academics relative to their male colleagues. This gender gap has come under increased focus as universities take steps to foster diversity and inclusiveness. Bibliometrics can provide a window into the gender disparity in research by measuring the metadata of academic publications. By determining the ratio of female to male authors, the gender bias at the level of the institution can be quantified. This study examines the proportion of female authors of academic articles at thirty Canadian " ;
    lis:publishedIn lis:journal/canadian-journal-of-information-and-library-science ;
