    lis:citesCount 1 ;
    dcterms:description "Drawing on data from the qualitative survey study of avid immigrant and migrant Spanish-speaking readers residing in Canada and the U.S., this paper looks at their use of libraries, specifically, in the context of leisure reading. Acknowledging a gap in current research on Spanish-speaking immigrants/migrants, the study focuses on avid lifelong readers rather than information seekers, achieves an understanding of their reading practices and interactions with libraries in the context of their pre-migration experiences, and highlights readers’ suggestions for the improvement of collections, spac" ;
