    a lis:Article ;
    dcterms:title "Machine Translation in Scholarly Publishing" ;
    dcterms:issued "2025"^^xsd:gYear ;
    lis:citesCount 1 ;
    dcterms:description "English occupies a central position in scholarly publishing, but using a lingua franca for scholarly publishing has consequences for scholars, science, and society. For instance, non Anglophone researchers may need longer to read and write in English and may face more manuscript revisions and rejections, potentially leading to a lower volume of research output, which could negatively affect career advancement. To what extent can machine translation (MT) tools (e.g., Google Translate) help to support a more multilingual scholarly publishing ecosystem? To find out, we undertook a scoping review " ;
