    a lis:Article ;
    dcterms:title "A bibliometric study of the work of Rosalind E. Franklin (1920-1958)" ;
    dcterms:issued "2022"^^xsd:gYear ;
    lis:citesCount 0 ;
    dcterms:description "After a short introduction to her life and work, we construct Rosalind Franklin’s citation environment in the sense of Howard White. This environment consists of four groups of authors related to Franklin: her co-authors, those cited by Franklin, those co-cited with Franklin, and those citing Franklin. We further found two of her articles that can be considered as suffering from delayed recognition. The article ends with a complete bibliography of Franklin. Although she never received the Nobel Prize, she most certainly was “of Nobel Class.”" ;
