    dcterms:description "American Corners in the Philippines are strategically located within select academic libraries, where they design and implement programs based on the six core pillars of American Spaces. Managing these programs requires extensive collaboration with diverse stakeholders to ensure effectiveness and reach target audiences. As American Spaces cycle through program creation, planning, implementation, and evaluation, a critical question arises: how do they sustain partnerships and expand opportunities? This research focuses on understanding how these partnerships are formed, managed, and sustained, " ;
