    a lis:Article ;
    dcterms:title "Effectiveness of Vernacular Library Orientation Videos in Comparison with the English Language Equivalent" ;
    dcterms:issued "2020"^^xsd:gYear ;
    lis:citesCount 2 ;
    dcterms:description "Vernacular language videos with narration in non-English languages have been used in North American academic libraries to engage and empower international and non-native English-speaking students. This study investigated the effectiveness of McGill University Library’s orientation videos from the perspective of these students, using mixed methods to outline student learning, affective responses, and views on audiovisual features used in the video. Compared to the English video, vernacular language videos are equally effective in delivering content and more adept at invoking student enthusiasm " ;
